---
import BaseLayout from '@/components/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '@/components/Breadcrumbs.astro';

const updated = 'September 2026';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Terms of Use"
  description="The terms that govern your use of CryptoCards.biz."
>
  <Breadcrumbs items={[{ label: 'Home', href: '/' }, { label: 'Terms' }]} />
  <div class="container-page mt-6">
    <article class="prose-page max-w-3xl">
      <h1 class="text-3xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-slate-900 sm:text-4xl dark:text-white">
        Terms of use
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-4 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400">Last updated: {updated}</p>

      <h2>1. Information, not advice</h2>
      <p>
        The content on CryptoCards.biz is provided for general information only. It is not financial,
        legal or tax advice, and it is not a recommendation to buy, hold or sell any asset. You are
        responsible for your own decisions.
      </p>

      <h2>2. Accuracy</h2>
      <p>
        Crypto card fees, limits, availability and promotions change frequently. We work to keep
        listings accurate and show a last-verified date, but we cannot guarantee that every detail is
        current. Always confirm the terms with the provider before applying.
      </p>

      <h2>3. Third-party services</h2>
      <p>
        Links to crypto card providers are provided for convenience. We are not responsible for their
        products, services or terms. Your relationship with a provider is governed by that provider's
        own agreements.
      </p>

      <h2>4. Affiliate relationships</h2>
      <p>
        Some links are affiliate links and we may earn a commission. See our{' '}
        <a href="/affiliate-disclosure">affiliate disclosure</a> for details.
      </p>

      <h2>5. Limitation of liability</h2>
      <p>
        To the extent permitted by law, CryptoCards.biz is not liable for any loss arising from use of
        the site or reliance on its content.
      </p>

      <h2>6. Changes</h2>
      <p>We may update these terms from time to time. Continued use of the site means you accept the current version.</p>
    </article>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
